{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeCornerCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeCornerCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeExchange","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeUpOperator","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedPartitionShape","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRule"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_recurrence'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_recurrence'","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L350-L361","doc":"**The involution recurrence, unconditionally.**\n\n    s(n+2) = s(n+1) + (n+1)·s(n),      s(k) := Σ_{μ of size k} #SYT(μ),\n\nwith no hypothesis: `upOperatorIdentity_holds` discharges the one that\n`sum_numSYT_recurrence` carries.  This is exactly the recurrence defining the involution\nnumbers, `I(n+2) = I(n+1) + (n+1)·I(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L327-L348","doc":"**The involution recurrence, conditional on the up-operator identity.**\n\n    s(n+2) = s(n+1) + (n+1)·s(n),      s(k) := Σ_{μ of size k} #SYT(μ).\n\nThis is *exactly* the recurrence defining the involution numbers,\n`I(n+2) = I(n+1) + (n+1)·I(n)` (`QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC8SuperExpBound.involutionNumber`).\nWith matching base cases `s(0) = s(1) = 1` it gives `Σ_{λ⊢n} f^λ = I(n)` — the identity\nthat licenses reading the involution numbers as the `q = 1` na-Stokes period in\n`QOU.Mass.SWPeriodSuperExponential`, and the open target of beans `qou-m3xr` / `qou-jlam`.\n\n`UpOperatorIdentity` is discharged by `upOperatorIdentity_holds` above, so this theorem is\n**unconditional** — the hypothesis is kept in the signature for the callers that already\nthread it, and `sum_numSYT_recurrence'` below is the hypothesis-free form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_mul_corners_of_upOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_mul_corners_of_upOperator","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L282-L324","doc":"**The weighted corner sum, reduced.** Given the up-operator identity, the corner-weighted\nrank sum is exactly `(n+1)·s(n)` — which is the coefficient the involution recurrence needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.upOperatorIdentity_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.upOperatorIdentity_holds","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L275-L279","doc":"**`UpOperatorIdentity` holds** — it is `QOU.Mathlib.upSum_eq` transported from the\n`Finset` sum to the subtype sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_subtype_addable_eq_upSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_subtype_addable_eq_upSum","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L263-L273","doc":"The subtype sum over addable cells is `upSum`, which sums over the `Finset`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.UpOperatorIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.UpOperatorIdentity","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L254-L261","doc":"**The up-operator identity of Young's lattice**, as a named `Prop`.\n`Σ_{λ = μ + box} #SYT(λ) = (|μ| + 1)·#SYT(μ)`.  Discharged by `upOperatorIdentity_holds`\njust below; it is a definition rather than a plain theorem statement only so that the\nconsumers below can carry it as an explicit hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_succ_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_succ_split","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L203-L236","doc":"**The recurrence's shape.** Feeding the differential property `a(ν) = r(ν) + 1` into\nthe weighted exchange splits it:\n\n    s(n+1) = s(n) + Σ_{ν of size n} #SYT(ν) · r(ν).\n\nCompare the involution recurrence `I(n+2) = I(n+1) + (n+1)·I(n)`. The two agree exactly\nwhen `Σ_ν #SYT(ν)·r(ν) = n · s(n-1)` — the one step still open, and now the *only* thing\nbetween this file and `Σ_λ f^λ = I(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_numSYT_succ","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L150-L201","doc":"**The weighted rank exchange.** Summing `#SYT` over a whole rank equals summing, one\nrank down, `#SYT ν` times the number of addable cells of `ν`:\n\n    s(n+1) = Σ_{ν of size n} #SYT(ν) · a(ν).\n\nThe left side is the branching rule summed over the rank; the right side is the same sum\nreindexed by `cornerAddEquiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rankExchange_fst_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rankExchange_fst_fst","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L145-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rankExchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rankExchange","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L137-L143","doc":"The rank exchange as a single equiv of sigma types: `cornerAddEquiv` with both sides\nregrouped by diagram. Kept as a top-level `def` (rather than a `have` inside the proof)\nso that the weight-matching step can unfold it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sizedAddPairSigma'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sizedAddPairSigma'","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L128-L135","doc":"`SizedAddPair n` as a sigma, indexed by `IsAddableCell`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sizedCornerPairSigma'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sizedCornerPairSigma'","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L119-L126","doc":"`SizedCornerPair n` as a sigma, indexed by the branching theorem's corner subtype. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.fintypeAddableSubtype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.fintypeAddableSubtype","kind":"instance","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L112-L117","doc":"Addable cells of a fixed diagram form a `Fintype`, via `addableCells`. (The corner\ncounterpart already exists as `SYTBranchingRule.fintypeCorners`; there is no competing\ninstance for the addable side.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_cornerCells_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_cornerCells_succ","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L91-L102","doc":"**The differential form of the rank exchange.** Feeding `a(ν) = r(ν) + 1` into the\nright-hand side: the corner count at size `n+1` exceeds that at size `n` by exactly the\nnumber of diagrams of size `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_cornerCells_succ_eq_sum_addableCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_cornerCells_succ_eq_sum_addableCells","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L76-L89","doc":"**The rank-level exchange.** Summed over a whole rank, the number of removable\ncorners at size `n+1` equals the number of addable cells at size `n`. This is\n`cornerAddEquiv` with both sides regrouped by diagram and counted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sizedAddPairSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sizedAddPairSigma","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L67-L74","doc":"`SizedAddPair n` regrouped as a sigma over the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sizedCornerPairSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sizedCornerPairSigma","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L58-L65","doc":"`SizedCornerPair n` regrouped as a sigma over the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.fintypeSizedDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.fintypeSizedDiagram","kind":"instance","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeCornerCount.lean#L52-L56","doc":"Diagrams of a fixed size form a `Fintype`, transported from `Nat.Partition n` along\n`partitionShapeEquiv`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}